Appendix A — SPP Field Notation Reference

The abbreviated field notation used in LangOne transmission annotations throughout this document follows this convention:

• Singulon(x): A point-localized field excitation anchoring concept x
• FluxRegion(x): An extended field configuration representing concept x in a distributed, contextual form
• GradientFlow(x→y): A directed field transition from concept x to concept y
• ResonanceLattice(x): A periodic field structure encoding the temporal or structural pattern of x
• NullManifold(x): An enforced quiescence region suppressing concept x from the active field
• TensorBond(x×y): A cross-domain correlation structure linking concept fields x and y
• ResonanceCoupling(A ⊕ B): Superposition of fields A and B with resonance interaction term
• AttractorBinding(x AND y): A field configuration satisfying both x and y simultaneously

