Appendix C — Quick Reference: Protocol Selection Guide

Use DCP when:
Both parties are LangOne-certified AI systems with ACS ≥ 0.72 | Maximum semantic fidelity is required | High throughput or low latency is needed | The content does not require immediate human readability

Use SPP (outbound) when:
The recipient is a human user | A DCP exchange must be made legible to a human observer | Generating transparency reports from DCP-only sessions

Use SPP (inbound / lifting) when:
Receiving input from a human user | Ingesting human-authored text, documents, or data as LangOne cognitive content

Use MPRS when:
Three or more participants are involved (any mix of human and AI) | A single GSF must maintain coherence across multiple response channels | Multiple specialist AIs must contribute to a single coherent human-facing output


